Create a Python program that organizes files from a folder based on their extensions.

For example
photo.jpg → Images/
notes.txt → Text/
report.pdf → Documents/
data.csv → Data/

Create separate modules for file detection, file movement, logging, and exception handling.
Your program must handle situations such as a file not existing, destination folder missing, duplicate filenames, permission errors, and unsupported file types.
Create at least one custom exception such as
class UnsupportedFileError(Exception)
pass
Every successful and failed file operation should be recorded in a log file.

Sample Input:
My Folder is having the following files in it
photo.jpg
notes.txt
report.pdf
data.csv
program.exe

Sample Output:
python .\main.py my_folder
photo.jpg moves to Images/ folder
notes.txt moves to Text/ folder
report.pdf moves to Documents/ folder
data.csv moves to Data/ folder
program.exe will not move to any directory as it is unsupported file type

Logs:
2026-09-12 18:10:43,915 - INFO - SUCCESS: Moved 'my_folder\data.csv' to 'my_folder\Data\data.csv'
2026-09-12 18:10:43,917 - INFO - SUCCESS: Moved 'my_folder\notes.txt' to 'my_folder\Text\notes.txt'
2026-09-12 18:10:43,918 - INFO - SUCCESS: Moved 'my_folder\photo.jpg' to 'my_folder\Images\photo.jpg'
2026-09-12 18:10:43,918 - ERROR - FAILED: Unsupported file type: .exe
2026-09-12 18:10:43,919 - INFO - SUCCESS: Moved 'my_folder\report.pdf' to 'my_folder\Documents\report.pdf'

